\subsection{Validation}

\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Convergence diagnostics.} 4 chains, 1{,}200 post-warmup draws each; no $\hat R > 1.01$ warnings across all parameters; effective sample sizes comfortably above thresholds for all reported effects.
  \item \textbf{LOSO validation.} Leave-one-season-out re-fitting yields per-season within-week weighted RMSE between 0.342 and 0.862 (mean 0.518), stable across eras and rules (Figure \ref{fig:m3-loso}); the fitted coefficients are not driven by any single season.
  \item \textbf{Sanity checks on the fan-channel response.} Shares sum to 1 within every one of the 335 season-weeks by construction; judge points' panel range (8--45) matches the show's 30-point maximum plus bonus/finale structures.
  \item \textbf{Convergence under the conservative-response choice.} Using $\bar v$ rather than full-draw imputation narrows effective CIs. The only decisively contrasted effect (age) remains decisive under a triple of alternative response constructions run as a robustness check; the two that cross zero remain ambiguous, which is the conservative outcome.
\end{itemize}

